"answer":"sell","correct":false},{"answer":"did sell","correct":false},{"answer":"sold","correct":true}],"id":"dropdown_6","type":"dropdown","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/WB\/unit_6\/p39_ex4\/"},{"additionalAnswers":[{"answer":"can make","correct":false},{"answer":"made","correct":false},{"answer":"make","correct":true}],"id":"dropdown_7","type":"dropdown","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/WB\/unit_6\/p39_ex4\/"},{"additionalAnswers":[{"answer":"reporter","correct":true},{"answer":"businessperson","correct":false},{"answer":"guide","correct":false}],"id":"dropdown_8","type":"dropdown","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/WB\/unit_6\/p39_ex4\/"},{"additionalAnswers":[{"answer":"can","correct":false},{"answer":"could","correct":true},{"answer":"was","correct":false}],"id":"dropdown_9","type":"dropdown","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/WB\/unit_6\/p39_ex4\/"}],"staticConfigs":[],"parts":["<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">For many people, being a <sup>1<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_0\"><\/dropdown> is a dream job. Why? On a podcast, you <sup>2<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_1\"><\/dropdown> talk about anything you like \u2013 something interesting \u2013 and people listen. You <sup>3<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_2\"><\/dropdown> be an expert. And with a laptop, most people can <sup>4<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_3\"><\/dropdown> make a podcast at home.<\/p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><br><\/p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">You can\u2019t always make money from podcasting, but many people do. And podcasts are popular.<\/p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">About 500 million people now <sup>5<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_4\"><\/dropdown> to them in more than 100 languages. There are at least 3 million podcasts you can choose from. That\u2019s a lot of podcasts! And every year, there are more podcasts, more podcasters and more listeners.<\/p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><br><\/p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">In the year 2000, you <sup>6<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_5\"><\/dropdown> be a podcaster.<\/p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Why not? Because \u2018podcaster\u2019 wasn\u2019t a word, and it wasn\u2019t a job. There couldn\u2019t be podcasts before Apple <sup>7<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_6\"><\/dropdown> the first iPod\u00ae personal music player in 2001. That\u2019s when a few people started to <sup>8<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_7\"><\/dropdown> shows and put them on the internet. But the first time someone used the word \u2018podcast\u2019 was in February 2004. A newspaper <sup>9<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_8\"><\/dropdown> named Ben Hammersley suggested the name for a new style of show \u2013 a type of radio programme for personal music players. \u2018Podcaster\u2019 <sup>10<\/sup> <dropdown id=\"dropdown_9\"><\/dropdown> only be a job after podcasts had a name!<\/p>"],"globalTypesConfigs":[{"type":"dropdown","shuffle":false,"widthMode":"adaptToContent"}]}]}